              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is just heavenly. I don't use the almonds, and I spoon plenty of apricot preserves over the brie before wrapping and I think this adds the extra kick it needs. Also, for those of you willing to try, this recipie works well with phyllo dough. Just brush melted butter over top of brie, then add preserves, and wrap in 4 sheets of phyllo that have also been brushed with butter. Trim excess dough and freeze. This is very important and should also be done with the puff pastry version. If you don't freeze, the cheese is completely liquid by the time the dough is done, and so this way they both come out perfect. Bake according to package directions."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe is fabulous!!! I filled mine with apricot preserves along with the almonds and brushed with egg whites as suggested! Thank you so much to Veronika for the tip on freezing before cooking! The pastry came out wonderfully cooked and the cheese was perfect! This was THE hit of our party!",
            "datePublished": "2001-12-28T17:53:25.357Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MOBIDDY02"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Perfect. I shaved off some of the rind, cut the brie in half, put apricot preserves in middle )like a brie/apricot sandwhich), warpped puff pastry around brie, trimmed extra pastry, used egg white wash all over pastry. Wrapped in plastic wrap and froze for 2 hours. Baked at 425 for 25 mins. Served with crackers, pears, apples, and bread. Made two of them for 12 people and there wasnt a drop left. Huge hit!",
            "datePublished": "2011-04-23T06:11:42.090Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Judy Campen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was delicious, but I made a few changes. I toasted the almond first, added dried cranberries to the filling. I also stuck it in the freezer for 1 hour before baking it so the brie &amp; filling wouldn't seep out of the crust. It turned out awesome!!",
            "datePublished": "2018-12-26T22:29:30.190Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "hulagirl34"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Turn the oven up to 400 and put the brie in the freezer for about an hour before putting in the oven. It's so it won't liquify before it gets brown. I made 2 kinds. One sweet with apricot preserves and the other with sautéed in butter till browned cremini and portabella mushrooms. Long time ago I went to a holiday party and they had the mushroom baked brie and it was so incredible. I had to give it a try this year and so surprised at how easy it is to make. So delicious to say the least. Husband loved both! Thank you for sharing.",
            "datePublished": "2024-12-18T19:52:45.410Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lutzflcat"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is good, but I think it’s missing a layer of flavor. The puff pastry baked up nicely, but the cheese flavor was very neutral. I drizzled some honey on the almonds before adding the top layer of brie, but I could see adding either some herbs for some savoriness or a layer of sweet preserves such as apricot or fig to brighten the flavor. I bumped up the temp at the end because it wasn't golden brown. Next time, I'll try baking at 375ºF. Certainly is quick to put together and has nice presentation.",
            "datePublished": "2023-12-23T11:09:05.250Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Crystal dalesandro"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I like this recipe as it is basic. I used homemade Fig jam and brushed the top with a white egg wash for extra color.",
            "datePublished": "2019-12-13T15:58:11.890Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Patty on the porch"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yum! I did read the reviews and did the following - froze brie for 30 minutes prior, added raspberry preserves, completely seal pastry, used the trimmings to cut shape for top, brushed with egg whites, upped oven to 400 for about 30 minutes. Thanks for sharing - easy app for party!",
            "datePublished": "2017-06-13T19:06:48.733Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
